# MCSP Semantic Dimensional Minimization 0.47

Status: Constructive semantic-safety experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent: TERMINAL-RELEASE-TRANSITION-CONTRACT-0.46

## Objective

MCSP SHALL minimize semantic commitment while preserving sufficient determination.

Preference relations:

    CONDITION before STATE
    MODE before TYPE

These are reduction/preferences, not claims that STATE or TYPE can never exist.

A stronger dimension SHALL NOT be introduced merely because a weaker dimension is
persistent, repeatedly processed, operationally useful, or convenient to name.

## CONDITION before STATE

When a determinate condition sufficiently excludes incompatible interpretations,
MCSP SHALL NOT require STATE.

Examples:

    CONDITION = IDLE
    CONDITION = PROCESSING
    CONDITION = TERMINAL_ATTACHED
    CONDITION = TERMINAL_RELEASE_CAPABLE

Persistence, repetition, observation, calculation, estimation, transition relevance,
or execution relevance do not by themselves promote CONDITION to STATE.

STATE may be considered only if a future requirement demonstrates a material
semantic distinction that cannot be preserved through determinate conditions.

## MODE before TYPE

When an operational/projection distinction can be expressed without asserting what
a construct intrinsically is, MCSP SHALL prefer MODE over TYPE.

Example:

    CONDITION = PROCESSING
    MODE = FOREGROUND

rather than requiring:

    TYPE = FOREGROUND_PROCESS

A later condition may be:

    CONDITION = PROCESSING
    MODE = BACKGROUND

without requiring a new TYPE.

TYPE may be considered only if a future requirement demonstrates a material
classification invariant that MODE cannot preserve.

## No automatic promotion

Forbidden automatic promotions:

    CONDITION -> STATE
    persistent CONDITION -> STATE
    changing CONDITION -> STATE
    MODE -> TYPE
    persistent MODE -> TYPE
    changing MODE -> TYPE

Processing a condition SHALL preserve its dimensional boundary unless explicit
qualified evidence establishes insufficiency.

## Safety rule

For every processed semantic record in this bounded model:

1. determine the required condition;
2. determine an applicable mode only when operational interpretation needs it;
3. test whether the resulting determination is sufficient;
4. leave STATE absent when CONDITION is sufficient;
5. leave TYPE absent when MODE is sufficient;
6. reject any unrequested promotion.

Absence of STATE or TYPE is not missing information when the weaker dimensions
already provide sufficient determination.

## Kernel

Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.

MODE is a derived semantic dimension above the kernel.
STATE remains derived and optional.
TYPE remains derived and optional.

Neither STATE nor TYPE is introduced as an operative dimension by 0.47.
